    <othernotes>Mina Targeting Guide:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At a glance:&lt;br&gt;-Mina's a young Korean-American woman in her 20s, who's had a pretty easy life and is obviously wealth.&lt;br&gt;-Mina's not particularly kind, but she can be very direct when something interests her.&lt;br&gt;-Mina is from New York City, 1949, the year of the Maelstrom, a massive conflux of occult magic and energy.&lt;br&gt;-Mina's familiar with magic and general pulpy spooky stuff.&lt;br&gt;-She's a vampire, though which rules apply to her are somewhat ambiguous.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notes:&lt;br&gt;-This takes place right before The Ritual, which is the event inside of Deadlock, and happens *once*, with the winners getting a wish. &lt;br&gt;-Mina's aware of her fellow Deadlock players, but has obviously not fought alongside them in the game yet. &lt;br&gt;-Mina and the Ha family are absurdly wealthy.&lt;br&gt;-Mina, as written, isn't quite as awful in reality as she tries to push herself to be. She's inconsiderate, stuck-up, and an all-round unlikable jerk, but she *is* trying to accomplish things on her own merits and it eats at her to wonder how much of her accomplishments are entirely due to her parents' money rather than her own aptitude.&lt;br&gt;-Deadlock's 1940s are more progressive than Real Life's 1940s, so most of her conflict is personality-driven or just unironically being anachronistic moreso than bigoted. (Her fiance, Arin, was nonbinary and she has never disrespected those pronouns, for instance.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Good Topics:&lt;br&gt;-Individual accomplishment&lt;br&gt;-AMERICA&lt;br&gt;-Fashion, especially if your character earnestly asks for advice&lt;br&gt;-Mina's actually not so rude to people that are nice to her. She's not likely to take kindness for granted, even if she expects it.&lt;br&gt;-Vampire society&lt;br&gt;-Mina's own goals&lt;br&gt;-Spicy: Mina was due to be married, and her fiance got assassinated. This ruined her life, in her eyes, and she blames the fiance for being assassinated. As such, Mina's never really experienced intimacy with another person.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notes:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Good topics:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Next:&lt;br&gt;-SPLICE THE LOOKBOOK&lt;br&gt;-Targets/fixes&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Postlive:&lt;br&gt;-Use single compressed when she's on main&lt;br&gt;-use noyourethejoke, vamp, and insatiable when shes on main</othernotes>
